/-!
# Second-normalizer prime-degree exclusions for J₁, J₄ and Rudvalis

Order divisibility of the actual smaller PSL₂ two-core section bounds its
field degree by five in J₄ and six in Ru. Hence the full natural plane,
including C_V(L), has binary dimension at most fifteen or eighteen.
The two carrier orders contain 37 and 29, whose binary multiplicative
orders are 36 and 28. Cubic rank two and the inherited SQTK hypotheses
make the containing component's two-core quotient quasisimple. Perfectness
then makes K generated by the indicated prime-elements, so its action on
the original small plane is trivial. This contradicts the literal natural
L₂ action without requiring faithfulness on K or irreducibility of full V₂.
The existing J₁ field-four comparison and actual simplicity give the same
contradiction with prime nineteen and its binary multiplicative order eighteen.

The source quotient and natural-cover maps belong to
qt-d-1222-natural-flag-cartan and are discharged by
qt-d-1222-natural-local-geometry. This module discharges both owned
second-refinement rows without an exhaustive embedding-list premise.
The relative-components owner retains first-index embeddings, other
refinement rows and the field-four triangle.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith 11.0.3, 11.1.1--11.1.2 and G.7.1,
printed pp.760--765,347, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004.
The imported concrete carriers retain their source attribution and licenses.
-/

public noncomputable section
open Subgroup Theory.GroupTheory Representation
